## electromagnetic-induction

electromagnetic-induction-ask = When does a current flow in the coil?
electromagnetic-induction-title = A magnet and a coil: electromagnetic induction
electromagnetic-induction-choices = When the magnet and the coil move against each other
electromagnetic-induction-choices-2 = When the magnet lies in the coil
electromagnetic-induction-choices-3 = A magnet makes no current
electromagnetic-induction-turns-label = Turns in the coil
electromagnetic-induction-turns-options = 100
electromagnetic-induction-turns-options-2 = 200
electromagnetic-induction-turns-options-3 = 400
electromagnetic-induction-build-question = We join a coil of { $turns } turns to a milliammeter with its zero in the middle: the needle swings the way the current goes. We put a bar magnet in the coil; then pull it out fast and push it in fast, north pole first, then slowly, and then push it in fast south pole first. At last we keep the magnet still and slip the coil onto it fast. Each time we note which way and how far the needle swung. When does a current flow in the coil?
electromagnetic-induction-setup = A coil, a bar magnet, a milliammeter with its zero in the middle, connecting wires
